# COMPONENT

## EventDriven

### PACKAGE

org.sample.eventdriven

### DESCRIPTION

Minimal event-driven sample component.

### SPECIFICATION

This component emits one event, receives it through CNCF event reception,
and exposes the visible effect through a query.

# SERVICE

## Event

### DESCRIPTION

Event emission and observation operations.

### OPERATION

#### emitEvent

##### DESCRIPTION

Emits the `item.changed` event.

##### IN

name, title

##### OUT

Event emission result.

#### recordEffect

##### DESCRIPTION

Receives the emitted event and records the visible effect.

##### IN

event payload

##### OUT

Recorded effect.

#### loadEffect

##### DESCRIPTION

Reads the current post-event effect.

##### IN

None.

##### OUT

Recorded effect.

# ENTITY

## Item

### DESCRIPTION

Minimal entity used so the sample remains a generated component rather than a handwritten provider.

### ATTRIBUTE

| name  | type     | multiplicity |
|-------+----------+--------------|
| id    | entityid | 1            |
| name  | name     | 1            |
| title | string   | 1            |

# COMMAND

## EmitEvent

### DESCRIPTION

Command to emit the `item.changed` event.

### ATTRIBUTE

| name  | type   | multiplicity |
|-------+--------+--------------|
| name  | name   | 1            |
| title | string | 1            |

## RecordEffect

### DESCRIPTION

Command to record the received event effect.

### ATTRIBUTE

| name  | type   | multiplicity |
|-------+--------+--------------|
| name  | name   | 1            |
| title | string | 1            |

# QUERY

## LoadEffect

### DESCRIPTION

Query to read the current visible effect.

# OPERATION

## emitEvent

### TYPE
COMMAND

### IMPLEMENTATION
event-emit

### INPUT
EmitEvent

### OUTPUT
EmitEventResult

## recordEffect

### TYPE
COMMAND

### EXECUTION
sync

### IMPLEMENTATION
event-effect-record

### INPUT
RecordEffect

### OUTPUT
RecordEffectResult

## loadEffect

### TYPE
QUERY

### IMPLEMENTATION
event-effect-load

### INPUT
LoadEffect

### OUTPUT
LoadEffectResult

# EVENT

## item.changed
- CATEGORY :: ActionEvent
- KIND :: changed
- SELECTOR :: source=event-driven
- ACTION_NAME :: event-driven.event.record-effect
- PRIORITY :: 0
